<!--
  RM_Krannock.xml                                      GREENTIDE_CANOPY_SWARM_1

  The Greentide's canopy-hazard insect axis. Owner ruling (question card,
  2026-09-25, on GREENTIDE_RISK_REWARD_EXCHANGE_1's Q3): the canopy-hazard
  insects are a NEW canopy swarm layer — new creature + art + behaviour — not
  folded into the existing 27-row WildAnimals_Greentide.xml cast, and NOT
  RM_Skerrel/RM_SkerrelGall (the sting-stacking gall wasp of
  GREENTIDE_WASP_SWARM_1 — a separate, already-designed item; do not conflate).

  ── Design card (this pass IS the design sitting — owner AFK, FOUNDRY's own
     call per the item's "author nothing before the design pass" instruction) ──

  Silhouette: large (baseBodySize 1.6 — bigger than RM_Quarrok's 1.4, well
  past ordinary vermin scale), armoured, insectoid. Per the ruling's own
  wording ("canopy-hazard... canopy is dangerous overhead") it is a canopy
  flier, not a ground-walker like Quarrok/Webwork's cast — it works trunks
  from the ground when it descends, but lives and travels through the high
  canopy between trees.

  Tier: RM_ (invented, franchise-free). Nothing about "a forest-hazard
  insect that chews tree bases" is Star Wars IP — per §7/Q11a, an invented
  exotic name stays RM_ tier unless it is GENUINE canon vocabulary. Checked
  the candidate against the Wookieepedia search API before finalizing
  (curl "https://starwars.fandom.com/api.php?action=query&list=search&srsearch=Krannock&format=json"
  → {"query":{"search":[]}}, zero hits, 2026-09-29) — also checked Vrelk,
  Chakrith, Gnashwing (all zero hits) before settling on Krannock. No
  collision anywhere in this repo either (grep -ri krannock: zero hits before
  this file).

  Solo vs. group: GROUP — wildGroupSize 3~6. The item's own title
  ("CANOPY_SWARM") is itself the strongest signal here: this is not a lone
  apex predator, it is a dispersed working party that shows up a few at a
  time and leaves a changed forest behind it. lifeStageAges reuses vanilla's
  EusocialInsectLarva/Juvenile/Adult (Locust/Megaspider's own stages) rather
  than inventing new ones — "eusocial" fits a swarm-behaviour insect exactly
  and needs no new LifeStageDef.

  Which mechanic(s): GNAWER ONLY, explicitly, not both — settling the
  ambiguity the item itself flags ("the design pass's own audit found the
  Gnawer/Shatterer split ambiguous... settle that explicitly rather than
  defaulting to 'one creature does everything' without saying so"). Reasons,
  stated plainly:
    1. RM_JobGiver_GnawTreeBase / RM_JobDriver_GnawTreeBase / the
       RM_GnawTreeBaseExtension marker are a complete, already-built,
       already-consumed pattern (RM_Quarrok's own RM_ChewAnchorsConsumerExtension
       is the structural precedent for "marker extension + inserted
       ThinkTreeDef splice, no new C#") — wiring Krannock to it is pure XML,
       zero new code, zero new risk.
    2. The Shatterer mechanic (fellsTreesBelowHealthFraction on
       HediffComp_PeriodicAreaAttack) has NO existing "grant this HediffDef
       permanently at spawn" wiring anywhere in this repo (checked: no
       hediffGiverSets pattern fits — that is a probabilistic disease roll,
       not "always has it"; no InnateHediff-shaped comp exists to reuse).
       Building one would be new mechanism-adjacent C# under an item whose
       own spec says "wire it to the existing mechanics, do not invent new
       ones" and whose constraints forbid any live/bridge proof of a new
       comp actually firing correctly. Forcing it in now would be the
       "default to one creature does everything, without saying so" failure
       the item explicitly warns against, wearing ambition as a disguise.
    3. The criteria line ("you hear trees falling in the canopy before you
       ever see what is doing it") is fully satisfied by Gnawer alone — a
       hidden insect chewing through trunks and dropping them is the whole
       image; nothing about it requires the Shatterer's area-damage aura too.
  ⇒ The Shatterer mechanic remains unwired to any creature after this item,
  exactly as it was before — a real, open follow-on (a second creature, or a
  later pass on this one) rather than something this item silently claimed.

  Flight: FLIES, for real — MaxFlightTime/FlightCooldown stat pair
  (Pawn_FlightTracker.CanEverFly), never a bool, per the standing rule ("if
  it flies in the fiction, it flies in the game") and copied from the
  vanilla Locust shape (Odyssey's own flying insect swarm animal — the
  closest vanilla analog to "canopy-hazard insect swarm" that exists) rather
  than invented from scratch. canLeaveMapFlying deliberately OMITTED, same
  posture as RM_Sivvern (Webwork) — it lairs in the Greentide canopy, no
  migration mechanism is claimed, so the narrow flier carve-out
  (BIOME_SPECIFIC_FAUNA_LAW_1) is not invoked. No flyingAnimationFramePathPrefix/
  -FrameCount: the flip-book frame set is OWED with the rest of this
  creature's art (see About.xml note on this item) — GetBestFlyAnimation
  returns null with none set and it flies plainly; never block flight
  waiting on frames.

  Roster placement: NOT done here, deliberately. Per the item's own
  instruction ("do NOT add it to WildAnimals_Greentide.xml's 27-row cast
  sweep... placement goes through the Greentide's own review sitting"), this
  def is real, valid and wireable but carries no commonality/band assignment
  and is not referenced from any BiomeDef's <wildAnimals> anywhere. It will
  not spawn on any map until that sitting places it.

  Meat/leather: useMeatFrom Megaspider, LeatherAmount 0 — same "no new
  generic-resource art owed" call the vanilla Locust itself makes (Odyssey's
  Races_Animal_Insect.xml), so this def needs no new meat/leather texture to
  be content-complete.

  Art: none exists. Searched infrastructure/artpipe/registry.jsonl,
  done/, _artsrc/ this pass for "canopy", "gnaw", "krannock" (all
  zero hits) — sanity-probed against "bloodymess" (24) and "greentide" (77)
  to confirm the search instrument itself works before trusting the zero.
  Queued via the normal fill_queue.py route:
  infrastructure/artpipe/art_lists/greentide_krannock.csv → RM_Krannock_v1
  (south/east/north, 256x256). Placeholder texPath below points at the owed
  location; never deploy against a donor texture for this creature — the
  swarm-flier-with-mandibles silhouette is the whole point.
-->
<Defs>

  <ThingDef ParentName="AnimalThingBase">
    <defName>RM_Krannock</defName>
    <label>krannock</label>
    <description>A slab-plated flying beetle the size of a dog, grey-green chitin dulled under a fur of moss and bark-dust, wings folded flat along its back until it drops out of the canopy onto a trunk it has already marked. It works alone or in a scattered handful, jaws built to grind through green wood in hours rather than days — you hear the trunk giving way long before you ever see what did it.</description>
    <statBases>
      <MoveSpeed>2.6</MoveSpeed>
      <MarketValue>90</MarketValue>
      <ComfyTemperatureMin>-10</ComfyTemperatureMin>
      <ArmorRating_Sharp>0.2</ArmorRating_Sharp>
      <ArmorRating_Blunt>0.1</ArmorRating_Blunt>
      <LeatherAmount>0</LeatherAmount>
      <Wildness>0.75</Wildness>
      <!-- Real flight, per the standing rule (owner, 2026-09-19). Core stat
           pair (Pawn_FlightTracker.CanEverFly), copied from vanilla Locust
           (Odyssey Races_Animal_Insect.xml) — the closest existing vanilla
           analog to a canopy-hazard insect swarm. -->
      <MaxFlightTime>9</MaxFlightTime>
      <FlightCooldown>5</FlightCooldown>
    </statBases>
    <tools>
      <li>
        <label>mandibles</label>
        <capacities>
          <li>Bite</li>
        </capacities>
        <power>11</power>
        <cooldownTime>2</cooldownTime>
        <linkedBodyPartsGroup>Mouth</linkedBodyPartsGroup>
      </li>
    </tools>
    <race>
      <body>BeetleLikeWithClaw</body>
      <baseBodySize>1.6</baseBodySize>
      <baseHealthScale>1.3</baseHealthScale>
      <baseHungerRate>0.28</baseHungerRate>
      <foodType>VegetarianRoughAnimal</foodType>
      <predator>false</predator>
      <fleshType>Insectoid</fleshType>
      <bloodDef>Filth_BloodInsect</bloodDef>
      <bloodSmearDef>Filth_BloodSmear</bloodSmearDef>
      <useMeatFrom>Megaspider</useMeatFrom>
      <manhunterOnDamageChance>0.08</manhunterOnDamageChance>
      <trainability>None</trainability>
      <lifeExpectancy>9</lifeExpectancy>
      <gestationPeriodDays>8</gestationPeriodDays>
      <lifeStageAges>
        <li>
          <def>EusocialInsectLarva</def>
          <minAge>0</minAge>
        </li>
        <li>
          <def>EusocialInsectJuvenile</def>
          <minAge>0.12</minAge>
        </li>
        <li>
          <def>EusocialInsectAdult</def>
          <minAge>0.35</minAge>
        </li>
      </lifeStageAges>
      <soundMeleeHitPawn>Pawn_Melee_SmallScratch_HitPawn</soundMeleeHitPawn>
      <soundMeleeHitBuilding>Pawn_Melee_SmallScratch_HitBuilding</soundMeleeHitBuilding>
      <soundMeleeMiss>Pawn_Melee_SmallScratch_Miss</soundMeleeMiss>

      <!-- Real flight, vanilla Locust's own shape. canLeaveMapFlying
           deliberately OMITTED — it lairs in the Greentide canopy, no
           migration mechanism claimed (see header). -->
      <flightStartChanceOnJobStart>0.12</flightStartChanceOnJobStart>
      <flightSpeedFactor>2.3</flightSpeedFactor>
      <canFlyIntoMap>true</canFlyIntoMap>
    </race>
    <modExtensions>
      <!-- GREENTIDE_CANOPY_SWARM_1: gives RM_JobGiver_GnawTreeBase (shipped
           by GREENTIDE_MECHANICS_2 M6 feller 3 with no consumer race) its
           first consumer. Same presence-only idiom RM_Quarrok's own
           RM_ChewAnchorsConsumerExtension already established for this kit
           of globally-inserted JobGivers — no-op for any race that doesn't
           carry it. No MayRequire: same convention RM_Greatbole.xml already
           set for a modExtension from this same assembly (see this mod's
           own About.xml — mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards is now a
           declared dependency, fixing the gap that def's own comment
           described but didn't act on). -->
      <li Class="RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.RM_GnawTreeBaseExtension">
        <searchRadius>35</searchRadius>
        <chewTicksToFell>1800</chewTicksToFell>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
    <tradeTags>
      <li>AnimalUncommon</li>
    </tradeTags>
  </ThingDef>

  <PawnKindDef ParentName="AnimalKindBase">
    <defName>RM_Krannock</defName>
    <label>krannock</label>
    <race>RM_Krannock</race>
    <combatPower>35</combatPower>
    <canArriveManhunter>false</canArriveManhunter>
    <!-- GROUP, not solo — the "canopy SWARM" design call (see header): a
         dispersed working party, not a lone apex predator. -->
    <wildGroupSize>3~6</wildGroupSize>
    <ecoSystemWeight>0.15</ecoSystemWeight>
    <!-- No flyingAnimationFramePathPrefix/-FrameCount: the flip-book frame
         set is OWED with the rest of this creature's art (header).
         GetBestFlyAnimation returns null with none set and it flies
         plainly — never block flight waiting on frames. -->
    <lifeStages>
      <li>
        <bodyGraphicData>
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/RM_Krannock/RM_Krannock</texPath>
          <graphicClass>Graphic_Multi</graphicClass>
          <drawSize>0.7</drawSize>
        </bodyGraphicData>
      </li>
      <li>
        <bodyGraphicData>
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/RM_Krannock/RM_Krannock</texPath>
          <graphicClass>Graphic_Multi</graphicClass>
          <drawSize>1.0</drawSize>
        </bodyGraphicData>
      </li>
      <li>
        <bodyGraphicData>
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/RM_Krannock/RM_Krannock</texPath>
          <graphicClass>Graphic_Multi</graphicClass>
          <drawSize>1.3</drawSize>
        </bodyGraphicData>
      </li>
    </lifeStages>
  </PawnKindDef>

</Defs>
